111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 86 0 R
/T (A strategy that may seem statistically significant may prove to be unprofitable once brokerage charges, taxes, slippage, and other market frictions are considered. The primary objective of this study is to determine whether the excess return associated with overnight price movements remains economically meaningful after accounting for implementation costs [9]. By focusing on the index futures markets, rather than solely focusing on the return pattern, this paper contributes to the literature on market anomalies by bridging the gap between statistical evidence and practical investment application.)
/E (A strategy that may seem statistically significant may prove to be unprofitable once brokerage charges, taxes, slippage, and other market frictions are considered. The primary objective of this study is to determine whether the excess return associated with overnight price movements remains economically meaningful after accounting for implementation costs [9]. By focusing on the index futures markets, rather than solely focusing on the return pattern, this paper contributes to the literature on market anomalies by bridging the gap between statistical evidence and practical investment application.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
