/T (This study utilises daily OHCLV data of the NIFTY50 Index and NIFTY Index Futures, covering the period from 20 June 2020 to 21 June 2026, obtained from the website of the National Stock Exchange \(NSE\) of India. The sample period considered for this study spans a variety of market conditions, including the post-pandemic recovery, periods of elevated inflation and market correction, thereby providing a complete environment to test the robustness of this strategy. Furthermore, this study will use the nearest to maturity NIFTY Index Futures contract due to its liquidity and bid-ask spreads, and the positions are rolled over to the subsequent contract prior to expiry)
/E (This study utilises daily OHCLV data of the NIFTY50 Index and NIFTY Index Futures, covering the period from 20 June 2020 to 21 June 2026, obtained from the website of the National Stock Exchange \(NSE\) of India. The sample period considered for this study spans a variety of market conditions, including the post-pandemic recovery, periods of elevated inflation and market correction, thereby providing a complete environment to test the robustness of this strategy. Furthermore, this study will use the nearest to maturity NIFTY Index Futures contract due to its liquidity and bid-ask spreads, and the positions are rolled over to the subsequent contract prior to expiry)
