<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (The result indicates that the systematic exploitation of overnight price movement produced superior absolute returns over the sample period. The performance is further reflected in its annualised return characteristics. The overnight strategy achieved a CAGR of 27.47%, compared to 15.09% for the benchmark portfolio. Although the strategy exhibited higher annualized volatility \(19.54% versus 15.47%\), it generated considerably greater returns per unit of risk, as evidenced by its Sharpe ratio of 1.01. From a downside risk perspective, the strategy demonstrated good resiliency. The maximum drawdown experienced by the overnight strategy was -16.02%, marginally lower than the -17.90% observed for the benchmark portfolio. Additionally, the strategy exhibited improved capital preservation characteristics during periods of market stress.)
/E (The result indicates that the systematic exploitation of overnight price movement produced superior absolute returns over the sample period. The performance is further reflected in its annualised return characteristics. The overnight strategy achieved a CAGR of 27.47%, compared to 15.09% for the benchmark portfolio. Although the strategy exhibited higher annualized volatility \(19.54% versus 15.47%\), it generated considerably greater returns per unit of risk, as evidenced by its Sharpe ratio of 1.01. From a downside risk perspective, the strategy demonstrated good resiliency. The maximum drawdown experienced by the overnight strategy was -16.02%, marginally lower than the -17.90% observed for the benchmark portfolio. Additionally, the strategy exhibited improved capital preservation characteristics during periods of market stress.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [20]
>>
