/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (The results are consistent with international literature documenting the dominance of overnight returns in equity markets. However, unlike previous studies that focused only on the statistical significance [12], the present study demonstrates how this anomaly could be exploited economically by a futures-based implementation, which remains profitable after incorporating market frictions. These findings challenge the market efficiency and suggest that information is incorporated into prices primarily during non-trading periods.)
/E (The results are consistent with international literature documenting the dominance of overnight returns in equity markets. However, unlike previous studies that focused only on the statistical significance [12], the present study demonstrates how this anomaly could be exploited economically by a futures-based implementation, which remains profitable after incorporating market frictions. These findings challenge the market efficiency and suggest that information is incorporated into prices primarily during non-trading periods.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [36]
>>
