275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 92 0 R
/T (This study examined the existence and practical exploitability of the overnight return anomaly [12] in the Indian equity market. Analysis revealed that a significantly large share of cumulative market returns was generated during non-trading hours, while intraday returns contributed negatively over the sample period.  Based on this evidence, a systematic trading strategy was implemented using NIFTY Index Futures to capture overnight price movements. The results demonstrate that the proposed strategy substantially outperformed a passive buy-and-hold investment by 194.5%. Additionally, the strategy demonstrated superior risk-adjusted returns. Importantly, these results remain profitable after incorporating transaction charges and market frictions, suggesting that this anomaly is not merely a statistical irregularity but an economically exploitable market inefficiency.  )
/E (This study examined the existence and practical exploitability of the overnight return anomaly [12] in the Indian equity market. Analysis revealed that a significantly large share of cumulative market returns was generated during non-trading hours, while intraday returns contributed negatively over the sample period.  Based on this evidence, a systematic trading strategy was implemented using NIFTY Index Futures to capture overnight price movements. The results demonstrate that the proposed strategy substantially outperformed a passive buy-and-hold investment by 194.5%. Additionally, the strategy demonstrated superior risk-adjusted returns. Importantly, these results remain profitable after incorporating transaction charges and market frictions, suggesting that this anomaly is not merely a statistical irregularity but an economically exploitable market inefficiency.  )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
