587 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Efficient Market Hypothesis states that asset prices fully reflect all available information, making it near impossible for any individual to generate abnormal risk-adjusted returns [2]. Still, decades of empirical research have documented persistent anomalies [3] that are inconsistent with the above hypothesis. Such anomalies have attracted considerable academic attention because they challenge traditional pricing theories, potentially paving the way for opportunities to develop systematic trading strategies. Traditional studies evaluate daily returns without distinguishing between trading and non-trading hours. More recent research decomposes total daily returns into overnight and intraday components [10]:)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 451 0 R
/Next 634 0 R
>>
