/Title (This study examines the practical exploitability of the overnight market anomaly in Indian equity markets using index futures. While prior research [4][12] suggests that most equity returns are generated outside trading hours, the economic viability remains uncertain once transaction costs, slippage, and taxes are accounted for. Using the past six-year historical data of the NIFTY future contracts to backtest a systematic trading strategy that maintains long exposure exclusively during overnight periods, entering positions near the market close and exiting them at the subsequent market open. The analysis incorporates realistic assumptions surrounding leverage, margin requirements, transaction costs [9], slippage, and statutory charges in the Indian derivatives market. The performance of the strategy is evaluated relative to a passive buy-and-hold exposure to the NIFTY Index and assessed using cumulative returns, volatility, Sharpe ratio [11], maximum drawdown [8], and risk-adjusted performance measures. The result provides evidence on the extent to which overnight returns contribute to the Indian equity market and whether this strategy can survive realistic market friction. The study further describes the practical challenges in converting a documented anomaly into an investment strategy)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 631 0 R
/Next 710 0 R
>>
