712 0 obj
<<
/Title (Multiple bodies of academic literature have documented the existence of systematic differences between overnight and intraday returns on US equities and ETFs [7]; however, the extent to which such patterns persist across different market structures and geographical regions remains an active area of research. To examine whether similar return dynamics are present in the Indian market, this study analyzes the performance of the NIFTY 50 Index by segregating total returns into overnight and intraday components. The analysis seeks to determine whether overnight returns account for a disproportionate share of overall market performance and whether such returns can be practically captured through a futures-based trading strategy)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 451 0 R
/Prev 717 0 R
/First 718 0 R
/Last 719 0 R
/Count -3
/Next 684 0 R
>>
endobj
713 0 obj
<<
/Title (To ensure that the results are not driven by extraordinary market conditions or institutional features unrelated to the overnight anomaly, certain trading days referred to as event days are excluded from the analysis. Major events like the general election result and other macroeconomic events that generate unusual price movements are omitted. Thursdays are also omitted from our analysis, due to elevated volatility and artificial price movements as a result of option expiry-related positioning and contract settlement effects.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 688 0 R
>>
endobj
