741 0 obj
<<
/Title (This study examined the existence and practical exploitability of the overnight return anomaly [12] in the Indian equity market. Analysis revealed that a significantly large share of cumulative market returns was generated during non-trading hours, while intraday returns contributed negatively over the sample period.  Based on this evidence, a systematic trading strategy was implemented using NIFTY Index Futures to capture overnight price movements. The results demonstrate that the proposed strategy substantially outperformed a passive buy-and-hold investment by 194.5%. Additionally, the strategy demonstrated superior risk-adjusted returns. Importantly, these results remain profitable after incorporating transaction charges and market frictions, suggesting that this anomaly is not merely a statistical irregularity but an economically exploitable market inefficiency.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 733 0 R
/Next 742 0 R
>>
endobj
