760 0 obj
<<
/Title (Having established the empirical existence of the overnight market anomaly and the construction of a systematic futures-based trading strategy to capture it, this section presents the results of the backtest, evaluating the profitability, risk, and economic significance of the strategy while comparing it with the performance of a passive investment in the NIFTY 50 Index)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 750 0 R
/Next 772 0 R
>>
endobj
761 0 obj
<<
/Title (The result indicates that the systematic exploitation of overnight price movement produced superior absolute returns over the sample period. The performance is further reflected in its annualised return characteristics. The overnight strategy achieved a CAGR of 27.47%, compared to 15.09% for the benchmark portfolio. Although the strategy exhibited higher annualized volatility \(19.54% versus 15.47%\), it generated considerably greater returns per unit of risk, as evidenced by its Sharpe ratio of 1.01. From a downside risk perspective, the strategy demonstrated good resiliency. The maximum drawdown experienced by the overnight strategy was -16.02%, marginally lower than the -17.90% observed for the benchmark portfolio. Additionally, the strategy exhibited improved capital preservation characteristics during periods of market stress.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 750 0 R
/Prev 773 0 R
>>
endobj
